<title>GERMANY: TABLE - Pan-German June ind. output rises 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Pan-German June ind. output rises 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT June 97	   May 97     June 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +1.4	 -1.5 (-0.2)    +0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.4	 +0.2 (+1.5)    unch</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     100.7	 99.3 (100.6)   99.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously announced data in parentheses.</p>
<p>The Economics Ministry said it expected the preliminary industry output data for June to be revised noticeably upwards.</p>
<p>The ministry also said the disparity between national data and figures for west and east Germany was due to differences in weighting data. Pan-German data are based on European Union statistical methods, which uses gross value added for weighting purposes, while regional data is based on net production value.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				   June 97		   May 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			75.1	+1.3	74.1	-6.3</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    99.8	+1.2	98.6	-1.3</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   105.1	+1.0     104.1	-1.0</p>
<p>	Capital goods     100.0	+2.9	97.2	-2.2</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  85.6	+5.2	81.4	-5.9</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     93.6	-3.9	97.4	+2.7</p>
<p> Energy output	    105.2	-2.4     107.8	+2.4</p>
<p> Construction	     113.6	+6.0     107.2	-4.9</p>
<p>Two month comparison May/Jun 1997 with Mar/Apr 1997:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     -0.5</p>
<p> Mining				    -1.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  -0.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   +0.5</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +0.5</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 -4.0</p>
<p> Energy output			   +2.5</p>
<p> Construction			    -2.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison May/Jun 97 with May/Jun 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.9</p>
<p> Mining				    -2.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +2.9</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   +5.3</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +3.6</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    -2.0</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -2.9</p>
<p> Energy output			   -0.8</p>
<p> Construction			    -9.8</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
